---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Public finance health
description: A wider set of public-finance and economic indicators, each with a neutral marker for which way it has moved.
eleventyComputed:
  dataUpdated: "{{ indicators.lastUpdated }}"
---
{% from "components/macros.njk" import caveatBox, sourceNote %}

{% set arrows = { "rising": "↑", "falling": "↓", "stable": "→" } %}

<div class="page-intro prose">
  <h1>Public finance health</h1>
  <p class="lede">Debt is only part of the picture. Here is a wider set of indicators, each showing which way it has moved lately.</p>
</div>

{{ caveatBox("The arrows show which way each figure has been moving recently, not whether that movement is good or bad. A rising tax burden or falling inflation can be read different ways depending on your view. This site shows the direction. The judgement is yours.", "Reading the arrows") }}

{% set groups = [
  { "title": "Public finances", "ids": ["debt-gdp", "borrowing-gdp", "interest", "tax-burden", "revenue", "spending"] },
  { "title": "The wider economy", "ids": ["inflation", "unemployment", "gdp-growth", "productivity"] }
] %}

{%- for g in groups %}
<h2 id="grp-{{ loop.index }}">{{ g.title }}</h2>
<ul class="indicator-grid" role="list">
    {%- for ind in indicators.indicators %}
      {%- if ind.id in g.ids %}
    <li><article class="indicator">
      <div class="indicator__head">
        <h3 class="indicator__name">{{ ind.name }}</h3>
        <dl class="status">
          <dt class="visually-hidden">Recent trend</dt> <dd><span class="status__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{ arrows[ind.status] }}</span> {{ ind.status }}</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      {%- if ind.unit.startsWith("£") %}
      <p class="indicator__value">£{{ ind.value | number }} <span class="indicator__unit">{{ ind.unit | replace("£ ", "") }}</span></p>
      {%- elif ind.unit.startsWith("%") %}
      <p class="indicator__value">{{ ind.value | number }}<span class="indicator__unit">{{ ind.unit }}</span></p>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="indicator__value">{{ ind.value | number }} <span class="indicator__unit">{{ ind.unit }}</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
      <p class="indicator__explain">{{ ind.explanation }}</p>
      {{ sourceNote(ind) }}
    </article></li>
      {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endfor %}

<details class="data-table-wrap">
  <summary>Show all indicators as a table</summary>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All indicators">
  <table class="data-table">
    <caption>Public finance and economic indicators. Last updated {{ indicators.lastUpdated | timeTag | safe }}.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Indicator</th><th scope="col" class="num">Latest</th><th scope="col">Trend</th><th scope="col">Confidence</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- for ind in indicators.indicators %}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">{{ ind.name }}</th>
        <td class="num">{% if ind.unit.startsWith("£") %}£{{ ind.value | number }} {{ ind.unit | replace("£ ", "") }}{% elif ind.unit.startsWith("%") %}{{ ind.value | number }}{{ ind.unit }}{% else %}{{ ind.value | number }} {{ ind.unit }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{{ ind.status }}</td>
        <td>{{ ind.confidence_level }}</td>
      </tr>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
</details>
